        {
          "claim_id": "claim:ad870033336df8652defd4150ae5734b9a582a1410c1730f20d838ff53d71f24",
          "clinical_approval": false,
          "evidence_ids": [
            "creatine-expansion-evidence:a79cc3b2266dbb7f40946ab9b7ec0907aec79d9c9ac0f5d6fa50500ee0ad2dfe",
            "creatine-expansion-evidence:0d67cd66bc81d156fc544d2b98905344f6b9cb8f7d9da2073e1e4d5f7256b396",
            "creatine-expansion-evidence:589c68ac830d2c74a68d2a45702afc3c5e89618661df6d08a9e5f1af706a3c20"
          ],
          "original_excerpt": "KIDNEY DYSFUNCTION\nTheoretically, taking creatine might worsen kidney dysfunction. Until more is known, use creatine with caution in patients with existing kidney dysfunction. Isolated case reports suggest that individuals with pre-existing kidney dysfunction may be at risk for worsening dysfunction with creatine supplementation (1368, 2118, 4576). However, this risk has not been evaluated in prospective clinical trials.",
